pve-fcsan (1.6.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * New array drivers: HPE Primera / Alletra 9000 / 3PAR (hpe-3par),
    HPE Alletra 5000/6000 and Nimble (hpe-nimble) and Dell Unity XT
    (dell-unity), each with array snapshots, copies and restore.
  * iSCSI provisioning: array setting protocol (fc, iscsi, both); nodes'
    initiator names registered on the array, nodes logged in to the
    array's target portals, portals restored at boot.
  * Array snapshots on NetApp ONTAP and IBM Spectrum Virtualize; Dell
    PowerStore datastores on several volumes snapshotted through volume
    groups.
  * Hardening: fc-discard uses the LVM plugin's background discard,
    fcsanvol disks release their LUN when the VM leaves a node, container
    restore from snapshot copies, no duplicate PVs on other nodes during
    snapshot mounts and DR imports.
  * Experimental: replication and disaster recovery (Pure FlashArray):
    recovery plans, test failover, failover and planned failover.

 -- pve-fcsan maintainers <maintainers@example.invalid>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

pve-fcsan (1.5.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Array snapshots of datastores (Pure FlashArray, InfiniBox, PowerStore):
    take, list and delete; mount a snapshot as a read-only copy datastore
    and restore one VM from it; roll a whole datastore back in place.
  * Snapshot schedules with retention (pvesan-snapshot.timer), weekly
    automatic space reclaim (pvesan-reclaim.timer) and the fc-discard
    storage option.
  * Monitoring: array view per datastore, I/O rates per LUN, datastore to
    VM lists, path health and array alerts through Proxmox VE notification
    targets (pvesan-monitor.timer), no_path_retry per LUN.
  * Node lifecycle: new nodes registered on arrays automatically; hosts of
    removed nodes can be removed. Zoning hints per node.
  * Experimental: storage type fcsanvol, one array volume per VM disk
    (Pure FlashArray only, raw disks only).

 -- pve-fcsan maintainers <maintainers@example.invalid>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

pve-fcsan (1.4.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * New array driver: Fujitsu ETERNUS DX S5 / AF S3 (and DX8100/8900 S4)
    through the ETERNUS RESTful API on port 5665 (controller firmware
    V11L40 or later). Each node HBA port is registered as an FC host and
    every volume is connected to all of them with one host LUN; volumes
    are created in thin provisioning pools.
  * README: a driver is optional; arrays without one work for everything
    except provisioning.

 -- pve-fcsan maintainers <maintainers@example.invalid>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000

pve-fcsan (1.3.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Fail-safe pve-manager integration: the line in PVE/API2/Nodes.pm now
    loads PVE::API2::SAN inside an eval, so a pve-fcsan that fails to load
    disables only /nodes/{node}/san (with a warning in the journal) instead
    of stopping pveproxy and pvedaemon. 'apply' replaces the 1.3.0 line.
  * pvesan-integrate status also checks that the API module loads and
    flags a line from an older pve-fcsan.
  * GUI: the PVE.panel.Config override catches its own errors, so a broken
    pvesan.js loses only the SAN panel.
  * Tests for pvesan-integrate against a fake pve-manager tree.

 -- pve-fcsan maintainers <maintainers@example.invalid>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

pve-fcsan (1.3.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * New array drivers, each checked against the vendor's own SDK/tooling:
    - Dell PowerStore (PyPowerStore)
    - Dell PowerMax / VMAX via Unisphere (PyU4V): host group, storage group
      and masking view per cluster
    - NetApp ONTAP (netapp.ontap Ansible collection): FlexVol + LUN per
      datastore, one FCP igroup per cluster
    - NetApp E-Series (SANtricity Ansible collection)
    - Hitachi VSP via Configuration Manager REST (OpenStack Cinder hbsd):
      host group and LU path per target port
  * Vendor settings on arrays: system-id, svm, portgroup, srp, slo,
    target-ports.
  * Provisioning reads the WWID after mapping where the array only reports
    it then (Hitachi).

